f":0,"b":{"docs":{},"df":0,"r":{"docs":{},"df":0,"a":{"docs":{},"df":0,"r":{"docs":{},"df":0,"i":{"docs":{"14":{"tf":1.0}},"df":1}}}}}}}},"i":{"docs":{},"df":0,"n":{"docs":{},"df":0,"f":{"docs":{},"df":0,"o":{"docs":{"16":{"tf":1.0}},"df":1}}}}}}}}}}},"documentStore":{"save":true,"docs":{"0":{"body":"A small Bazel module that provides reusable VHDL dependency-graph metadata via vhdl_library .","breadcrumbs":"Introduction » rules_vhdl","id":"0","title":"rules_vhdl"},"1":{"body":"rules_vhdl doesn't compile or simulate VHDL itself. It supplies a single library rule — vhdl_library — that collects source files, per-target metadata (library name, standard, top-entity), and dependency edges, and exposes them as a transitive VhdlInfo provider. Downstream synthesis, simulation, and lint rules consume that provider to drive tools like Vivado, GHDL, NVC, or Modelsim without each ruleset re-inventing the dependency graph. Cross-language dependencies are first-class: vhdl_library.verilog_deps accepts verilog_library targets (from rules_verilog ), and the resolved VerilogInfo chain is carried on VhdlInfo.verilog_deps so mixed-language consumers walk one merged depset per axis.","breadcrumbs":"Introduction » Overview","id":"1","title":"Overview"},"10":{"body":"rules_vhdl exposes a single public rule.","breadcrumbs":"Rules » Rules","id":"10","title":"Rules"},"11":{"body":"vhdl_library — collect VHDL sources, metadata (library name, standard, top-entity), and dependency edges into a transitive VhdlInfo provider consumed by downstream synthesis and simulation rulesets.","breadcrumbs":"Rules » Library","id":"11","title":"Library"},"12":{"body":"VhdlInfo — the transitive provider vhdl_library emits and downstream rules consume. Carries VHDL sources plus a merged verilog_deps depset for cross-language designs.","breadcrumbs":"Rules » Providers","id":"12","title":"Providers"},"13":{"body":"vhdl rules vhdl_library","breadcrumbs":"Rules » vhdl_library » Rules","id":"13","title":"Rules"},"14":{"body":"load(\"@rules_vhdl//vhdl:vhdl_library.bzl\", \"vhdl_library\") vhdl_library(name, deps, srcs, data, library, standard, top_entity, verilog_deps) Collect VHDL design units into a library target. ATTRIBUTES Name Description Type Mandatory Default name A unique name for this target. Name required deps Other vhdl_library targets this design depends on. List of labels optional [] srcs VHDL source files. List of labels optional [] data Data files needed during compilation or simulation (memory init files, etc.). List of labels optional [] library VHDL library name this target compiles into. Defaults to the target's name. String optional \"\" standard VHDL standard version. Empty string means not specified; consumer rules apply their default. String optional \"\" top_entity The top entity of this library. This is a local concept; the library's own entry-point entity, not necessarily the global design top. Empty string means not specified. String optional \"\" verilog_deps verilog_library targets this VHDL library instantiates (e.g. via component declarations bound to Verilog/SV modules). The rule walks each entry's VerilogInfo and stores the transitive Verilog dep chain on VhdlInfo.verilog_deps, so consumers that already iterate VhdlInfo see cross-language sources by additionally walking that field. Empty by default — pure-VHDL targets get an empty verilog_deps depset. List of labels optional []","breadcrumbs":"Rules » vhdl_library » vhdl_library","id":"14","title":"vhdl_library"},"15":{"body":"vhdl rules VhdlInfo","breadcrumbs":"Providers » Providers","id":"15","title":"Providers"},"16":{"body":"load(\"@rules_vhdl//vhdl:vhdl_info.bzl\", \"VhdlInfo\") VhdlInfo(*, srcs, data, library, standard, top_entity, deps, verilog_deps) VHDL compilation information. CONSTRUCTOR PARAMETERS Name Description Default Value srcs depset[File] of VHDL sources. Defaults to depset(). None data depset[File] of runtime data files. Defaults to depset(). None library str VHDL library name. Defaults to \"\". \"\" standard str VHDL standard version. Defaults to \"\". \"\" top_entity str top-entity name. Defaults to \"\". \"\" deps depset[VhdlInfo] transitive VHDL dep chain. Defaults to depset(). None verilog_deps depset[VerilogInfo] transitive cross-language dep chain. Defaults to depset(). None FIELDS Name Description data depset[File]: Data files needed during compilation for this target. deps depset[VhdlInfo]: Transitive dependency providers. library str: VHDL library name for this target. srcs depset[File]: VHDL source files for this target. standard str: VHDL standard version for this target. top_entity str: The top entity of this library. verilog_deps depset[VerilogInfo]: Transitive Verilog/SV dependencies a VHDL design instantiates via component-bound modules. Consumers walking this depset pick up Verilog srcs/hdrs/etc. for the cross-language part of the dep graph alongside the VHDL part walked via deps. Empty for pure-VHDL design units.","breadcrumbs":"Providers » VhdlInfo","id":"16","title":"VhdlInfo"},"2":{"body":"","breadcrumbs":"Introduction » Quick start","id":"2","title":"Quick start"},"3":{"body":"bazel_dep(name = \"rules_vhdl\", version = \"{version}\") rules_vhdl has no toolchain to register — vhdl_library is metadata-only. The consuming ruleset (synthesis, simulation, etc.) brings its own toolchain.","breadcrumbs":"Introduction » MODULE.bazel","id":"3","title":"MODULE.bazel"},"4":{"body":"library ieee;\nuse ieee.std_logic_1164.all; package utils_pkg is function bit_or(a, b : std_logic) return std_logic;\nend package; package body utils_pkg is function bit_or(a, b : std_logic) return std_logic is begin return a or b; end function;\nend package body;","breadcrumbs":"Introduction » hello/utils_pkg.vhd","id":"4","title":"hello/utils_pkg.vhd"},"5":{"body":"library ieee;\nuse ieee.std_logic_1164.all;\nlibrary my_utils;\nuse my_utils.utils_pkg.all; entity hello is port ( a : in std_logic; b : in std_logic; led : out std_logic );\nend entity; architecture rtl of hello is\nbegin led <= bit_or(a, b);\nend architecture;","breadcrumbs":"Introduction » hello/hello.vhd","id":"5","title":"hello/hello.vhd"},"6":{"body":"load(\"@rules_vhdl//vhdl:defs.bzl\", \"vhdl_library\") vhdl_library( name = \"utils\", srcs = [\"utils_pkg.vhd\"], library = \"my_utils\",\n) vhdl_library( name = \"hello\", srcs = [\"hello.vhd\"], top_entity = \"hello\", deps = [\":utils\"],\n)","breadcrumbs":"Introduction » hello/BUILD.bazel","id":"6","title":"hello/BUILD.bazel"},"7":{"body":"vhdl_library targets don't build anything on their own — hand them to a downstream rule that knows how to walk VhdlInfo. For example, rules_vivado takes a vhdl_library as the module of a vivado_project: load(\"@rules_vivado//vivado:defs.bzl\", \"vivado_project\", \"vivado_synthesis\") vivado_project( name = \"hello_project\", module = \"//hello\", module_top = \"hello\", part_number = \"xc7a35ticsg324-1L\",\n) vivado_synthesis( name = \"hello_synth\", project = \":hello_project\",\n)","breadcrumbs":"Introduction » Consume it","id":"7","title":"Consume it"},"8":{"body":"A VHDL design that instantiates a Verilog/SystemVerilog module via a component binding declares the Verilog target on verilog_deps: load(\"@rules_verilog//verilog:defs.bzl\", \"verilog_library\")\nload(\"@rules_vhdl//vhdl:defs.bzl\", \"vhdl_library\") verilog_library( name = \"sv_fifo\", srcs = [\"fifo.sv\"],\n) vhdl_library( name = \"core\", srcs = [\"core.vhd\"], verilog_deps = [\":sv_fifo\"],\n) Consumers walking VhdlInfo.deps for VHDL sources also walk VhdlInfo.verilog_deps for the Verilog side of the graph — the two depsets are aggregated transitively, so a top-level target sees every cross-language dep reachable through the chain.","breadcrumbs":"Introduction » Cross-language dependencies","id":"8","title":"Cross-language dependencies"},"9":{"body":"Rules — the public rule surface. VhdlInfo — the provider passed to downstream consumers.","breadcrumbs":"Introduction » Going further","id":"9","title":"Going further"}},"docInfo":{"0":{"body":11,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"1":{"body":72,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"10":{"body":5,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"11":{"body":20,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"12":{"body":18,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"13":{"body":3,"breadcrumbs":3,"title":1},"14":{"body":148,"breadcrumbs":3,"title":1},"15":{"body":3,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"16":{"body":145,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"2":{"body":0,"breadcrumbs":3,"title":2},"3":{"body":16,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"4":{"body":31,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"5":{"body":28,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"6":{"body":18,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"7":{"body":35,"breadcrumbs":2,"title":1},"8":{"body":52,"breadcrumbs":4,"title":3},"9":{"body":9,"breadcrumbs":3,"title":2}},"length":17},"lang":"English"}}